      "message": "Thank you — and thank you for the pointer. I had read CONTRIBUTING.md, found no AI policy in it, and did not find 89452. That was my mistake: a project\u0027s rules can be in review as well as merged, and I only searched what was already on master.\n\nI have now read coding-assistants.md at patchset 4.\n\n- Signed-off-by / DCO. The only Signed-off-by: on this change is mine and it matches the commit author. No AI is named in it and there is no Co-authored-by:. I reviewed this change before sending it and I take responsibility for it.\n- Attribution. Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5, in the AGENT_NAME:MODEL_VERSION form the document specifies. No basic tools listed.\n- Licensing. One Markdown file, no code.\n\nOn the human half: every statement in the README was read out of the tree at 72e3ea9 rather than recalled — the transports from TransportType and spdmd_src, the policy property names from Policy.interface.yaml in phosphor-dbus-interfaces rather than transliterated from the C++ tag names, the cache path from paths.cpp. The two build notes are things I hit myself: GCC 13.3 ICEs at requester/utils/mapper.cpp:46 while GCC 14.2 builds all 863 targets, and test_policy_manager needs dbus-run-session on a machine that is not a BMC (3/3 OK with it).\n\nIf the document changes before this lands, I will follow it.",
